Design a digital-to-analog converter (DAC) that translates a 4-bit digital input into a variable output voltage. The module utilizes a clock signal to synchronize updates, mapping the input to corresponding weight values for a weighted sum calculation. The output voltage is determined by scaling the reference voltage based on the selected weight and is updated every half sampling period, providing a smooth conversion from digital to analog values proportional to the input.
