description:
Design a pulse-width modulation (PWM) generator that produces a PWM output based on an 8-bit control input. The module operates on a clock signal and varies the duty cycle of the output waveform, which is calculated as a percentage of the maximum duty cycle (75%) based on the control input value. The PWM output is set high for a duration proportional to the duty cycle and low otherwise, creating a modulated signal suitable for controlling devices like motors or LEDs. The output frequency is determined by the specified width, set at 256 clock cycles.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [7:0] control,
  output pwm_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [7:0] control,
  output pwm_out
);parameter width = 256; // width of the PWM output waveform in clock cycles
parameter max_duty_cycle = 75; // maximum duty cycle of the output waveform, expressed as a percentage

reg [7:0] count = 0; // Initialize count
reg [7:0] duty_cycle;
reg pwm; // Changed from wire to reg

assign pwm_out = pwm;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (count == width - 1) begin
    count <= 0;
  end else begin
    count <= count + 1;
  end

  if (count < (width * duty_cycle / 100)) begin
    pwm <= 1;
  end else begin
    pwm <= 0;
  end
end

always @(control) begin
  duty_cycle <= max_duty_cycle * control / 255;
end

endmodule

