description:
Design a power-on reset (POR) circuit that generates a reset signal in response to a power supply condition. The circuit includes a 24-bit counter that increments on each clock edge. When the power supply signal (vdd) is low, the reset signal (rst) is asserted high, and the counter is reset to zero. Once vdd is restored, the counter counts until it reaches a predefined limit (100,000 cycles), at which point the reset signal is deasserted low, allowing the system to initialize. This module ensures a proper reset during power-up scenarios.
module top_module(
  input vdd, // power supply signal
  input clk, // clock signal
  output reg rst // reset signal
);

